  "name": "ANTI - CCP  TITRE (ANTI - CYCLIC CITRULLINATED PEPTIDE TITRE)",
  "code": "ACPT",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"711\" data-end=\"874\">\n<p data-start=\"713\" data-end=\"874\"><strong data-start=\"713\" data-end=\"738\">Negative (&lt; 20 U/mL):</strong> No significant level of Anti-CCP antibodies detected. Unlikely Rheumatoid Arthritis, though early/seronegative RA cannot be excluded.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"875\" data-end=\"1087\">\n<p data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"973\"><strong data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"902\">Positive (&gt; 20 U/mL):</strong> Presence of Anti-CCP antibodies, suggestive of Rheumatoid Arthritis.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"1087\">\n<li data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"1087\">\n<p data-start=\"978\" data-end=\"1087\">Higher titres correlate with increased likelihood of <strong data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1047\">RA diagnosis</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1052\" data-end=\"1084\">disease severity/progression</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1088\" data-end=\"1219\">\n<p data-start=\"1090\" data-end=\"1219\">Anti-CCP is <strong data-start=\"1102\" data-end=\"1128\">highly specific (~95%)</strong> for Rheumatoid Arthritis and helps differentiate RA from other inflammatory arthritides.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1337\">\n<p data-start=\"1222\" data-end=\"1337\">Should be interpreted in correlation with <strong data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1285\">clinical features</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1287\" data-end=\"1313\">RF (Rheumatoid Factor)</strong>, and imaging studies.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
